## 2026-11-27 00:50 — Talisman STRICT check PASSED (live service worker after real restart)
- `--remote-debugging-port` is IGNORED when `--user-data-dir` is the default profile dir.
- A plain symlink to the profile does NOT work (Chrome resolves it back to the default path).
- What WORKS: the FIRMLINK path, which is a distinct path string for the same bytes:
- Launch via `open -a "Google Chrome" --args ...` (LaunchServices). Direct exec of the binary FAILS with
- `chrome.management.getAll` is NOT a function inside the extension's own SW (only `chrome.management` object exists).
- Profile files (Secure Preferences, Local State, External Extensions dir, Local Extension Settings dir) are TCC-blocked
- Apple Events to Chrome is unreliable here: one hung `osascript` (e.g. `make new tab` at chrome://extensions) wedges
- Chrome was restarted twice during this check (by the agent). FINAL STATE: plain launch, 11 procs, NO debug flags,
## 2026-11-27 01:20 PST — Kibble watcher repair: /tmp purge root cause fixed
### Root cause (proven from the watcher's own log, /tmp/watch2.log)
- macOS purged /tmp: `/tmp/answers/` (6 batch-1 drafts) and `/tmp/answers/index.json` deleted.
